it's been five years half a decade since  breath of the wild released and guess  what yep you guessed it i've got more  things for you if you continue to enjoy  this series and want to see more from us  let us know with like alright here we go  one of the biggest new discoveries found  this year is item transmutation allowing  you to turn any material into something  else buy item hold smuggling five  materials into your hands selling the  rest off so you have none left it  carries over the holding 5 item's value  onto whatever stackable material you  want  including korok seeds and shrine orbs  this is the first discovery of srm also  known as stale reference manipulation in  breath of the wild although nothing  nearly as game breaking as something you  would see in ocarina of time  you've seen triforce designs everywhere  especially at the temple of time the  front and rear walls the floor it's  pretty hard to miss but there's one that  you might not have really seen if you  take a closer look at the floor of the  building in front of the temple there's  a signature of din the triforce of power  looking at the floor of the other two  you'll find barely legible symbols of  nehru and feyror as well these three on  the map all laid out show that this is  the full triforce symbol facing  southward pointing to the entrance of  the temple of time if you can't see the  symbols clearly in breath of the wild  hop on over to age of calamity you'll  see them there plain as day  you've probably heard the music and  shrines hundreds of times before but  have you actually paid attention to how  it works on the japanese nintendo  website they explain unlike most  standard songs that loop over and over  shrines have unique music with special  quote-unquote phrases that are  randomized over the time that you're  exploring that's why when you enter the  same shrine multiple times you'll  basically never hear the exact same song  over and over  [Music]  it's a little bit tricky but these goron  pots answer the age-old question of can  you pick up something you're standing on  yes if timed perfectly link will pick up  the pot he's standing on and launch  himself into the air although i don't  think that's how that works in real life  did you know that these types of candles  can be lit  many interactable torches in hyrule  castle come unlit and can give the  sanctum a really different vibe when all  of them are turned on  did you know that bloopies conduct  electricity  link has a high resistance to fire when  it's raining such as against burning  grass but this applies to other fire  effects as well such as during a flame  lizalfo's flame breath which will have  no effect on link  most players know that fire choo choo  and keys die when exposed to rain but  most people forget that choo choo  jellies are just portable water balloons  and when struck near them have the same  effect  when selling items the menu locks you  out of weapons bow and arrows and  shields never allowing you to sell these  items but believe it or not this  equipment does have ruby value in the  game's code these buying and selling  values were likely implemented during  testing then removed in the final  product but you can still see these  values in the game's code such as a  traveler's sword worth 5 rupees to sell  and 20 to buy the savage lionel bow  worth 52 rupees and 156 to buy and the  radiant shield worth 52 rupees and 210  rupees to buy this is more of a quick  tip but many players when trying to  start a fire on a hill throw the wood  first then try to quickly light it often  rolling away rather do it the other way  around shoot the ground with the fire  arrow first then throw the wood on top  of it  it's a much faster way to ignite the  wood or a funny trick is to hold smuggle  a burning weapon then throw the wood  it'll auto light as soon as it lands  here's an older trick some players don't  know it's possible to run around with  the horse permanently on ice or on fire  by using an old method of shooting your  own horse as you drown from gliding far  away or using the new campfire method  with enemy horses you can have the horse  permanently on fire or frozen this horse  just like with similar glitches makes  him immune to fire so if you have the  patience to get the horse to death  mountain you can ride around freely in  the burning air  everyone's heard of bullet time bounces  but you can do this to certain other  items besides link the easiest way is to  wait until a bokoblin lifts a rock then  freeze it in bullet time then watch the  fireworks unfold  everyone knows that you can fire bows  while on a horseback but what you may  not have noticed is that every bow is  changed to have the exact same fire rate  this can be a buff or a nerf depending  on the bow for example the royal guards  bow has the fastest fire rate in the  game and on horseback is nerfed pretty  severely while on the other hand the  ancient bow fires relatively slow but is  increased on horseback at the special  fire rate did you know that it's  possible to damage enemies with a  backflip this is more consistent with  low-level goblins with the well-timed  backflip you can take them out unarmed  terrytown's central bell is a unique  magnetic object try using magnesis on  the bell it will actually make a ringing  noise  or shooting it with projectiles to swing  it back and forth will work as well  there were many crystals and minerals in  breath of the wild including sapphire  ruby topaz diamonds and many more but  rivali carried one more stone that's  technically in the game but was never  usable jade rivale's hair ties and  anklets are made of pure jade but jade  is found nowhere else in hyrule  have you ever wondered how the grey  plateau tower had a gaping hole in the  hill when you first found it well  apparently during the calamity 100 years  ago guardians fired straight shots into  the mount making the hole that you see  today some people still haven't noticed  that during the champions ballad dlc  cutscenes the champions all perform  their signature key art pose at some  point  out of respect for our princess you may  keep your lives these poses are also the  chosen pose for all of the champion  amiibos the final design of the ancient  blade saw is based mostly on the rough  design of a chainsaw but during  development they had a slightly  different idea with three separately  rotating blades this was probably  inspired by the real life saw like this  in a profession called aerial tree  trimming where helicopters use these  multi-rotating blades to cut trees from  above  when you fire a shock or fire arrow at  an object it will carry those properties  for a moment with the object this counts  basically any object that can be shot  such as materials your own bombs and  even rupees which slide extremely far  and can carry your fire into enemy  territory  here's some nifty things that mentions  the final boss so spoiler heads up for  any recent new players i've shown before  with a lino's fireball so you can  counter it with any ice attack but this  includes many other fireball attacks  such as the wiz ropes fireballs fire  blight's normal and shotgun style  fireball and even calamity gannon's  deadly explosive fireball right out of  his hands  breath of the wild speedrunners have  drilled this 80 trick into their head  for years stun locking ganon with a  two-handed slam over and over to cheese  gannon but did you know that nintendo  completely knew about this trick and  wrote new codes around it with the  release of master mode this trick as  many know doesn't work on master mode  and only on normal mode because of this  specific set of code here ruling out  that if the hard code manager flag aka  master mode and other small conditions  are true stun lock is patched but if  it's false then this allows players to  stun ganon over and over why is this  stun lock purposely left in the game i'm  pretty sure papa nintendo is watching  the speedrunners  happy 5 year anniversary breath of the  wild hopefully the sequel will arrive  soon where we can continue the series on  there if you enjoyed this video we still  continue to make new videos about breath  of the wild to this day so stick around  for everything else gaming keep it here  on gamespot  you
 

